1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> A3: 99.99%<br /> A4: 99.99%<br /> A5: 92.28%<br /> N/A: 0,0000000003%<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:02:41-07:00","id":1408249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408235#post1408235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While they aren't going to apply to all Artifacts, any Artifacts that can benefit from Bracers of Universal Crafting should make things considerably easier.... what with the +3 dice over normal tools thing,</div> </div> </div> </div>Except those are Charm dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:42:34-07:00","id":1408263,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty okay with those numbers. Any time a DB wants to craft an artifact N/A it should be the kind of epic storyline that involves more than just comboing charms. At Essence 3 making a daiklave is pretty routine, but I don\u2019t think I\u2019d want people cranking out Stormcallers and Mela\u2019s Coils before Essence 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:57:55-07:00","id":1408269,"title":"","content":"A while back a did a similar set of calculations, but only assuming a level 1 stunt and without exceptional tools. As such I evaluated things a fair bit lower. As examples my E3 DB was succeeding on Artifact 3s 98.8% of the time, Artifact 4s 37.37% if the time and Artifact 5s only 0.29% of the time. That said my E5 DB was still successfully forging a 5 rated Artifact 84.96% of the time so even if you don't assume that exceptional tools for forging artifacts and level 2 stunts are easily available Artifact 5 is still clearly within the grasp of the greatest Dragon Blooded Exalted. And I was still assuming Willpower spent on every roll so it's not something that could be done casually.<br /> <br /> (My full list of results can be found in this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295348-lunar-craft-probabilities\">thread,</a> but I did make a mistake with the Artifact 2 calculations because I somehow had the threshold successes required as 25 in my head rather than 30 so those are off)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:04:04-07:00","id":1408271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408249#post1408249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except those are Charm dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't want to get into a debate over it, but even with Vance's answer in the Ask a Dev thread, that's very much going to be a table by table call. Vance's response was that such Artifacts count towards dice limits if they don't say otherwise, but didn't really add much guidance on what, &quot;compatible with Craft Charms,&quot; is supposed to mean in that regard since I don't think he was reading each Artifact independently when he answered.<br /> <br /> If you want to have DB crafters be able to eke out enough successes for upper level Artifacts it's a reasonable way to go about it. If you don't, it's a simple way to keep them from being able to too. Though the mote savings per roll would still be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:25:21-07:00","id":1408275,"title":"","content":"Is mote saving for rolls really worth it for craft ? I can't remember any time it was useful to track motes for crafting rolls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:41:54-07:00","id":1408277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408275#post1408275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is mote saving for rolls really worth it for craft ? I can't remember any time it was useful to track motes for crafting rolls</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, when you\u2019re doing long term downtime crafting no, when you\u2019re using Stone Shaping Fingers or Craftsmen Need No Tools to quickly whip up a solution to a problem where you might need those motes later, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:43:54-07:00","id":1408278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408275#post1408275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is mote saving for rolls really worth it for craft ? I can't remember any time it was useful to track motes for crafting rolls</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not for artifacts in most cases, where you're likely to be doing them mostly in downtime, and to have reasonably significant time periods between rolls, to build up craft XP and such. But they can be quite handy for mundane projects, when completing them on an adventure timescale is both more likely and more important. If you want to reinforce a fortress gate before the besiegers assault it, it's nice to have motes left over for the fight afterwards.<br /> <br /> And even artifacts can <i>potentially</i> benefit - if you've banked enough craft xp, there's no <i>technical</i> reason you can't just roll every single crafting roll one after the other, virtually instantaneously. If you're trying to finish the daiklave made from the bone of his corpse that you've just found in his tomb, while actually <i>fighting</i> the First and Forsaken Lion, saving those motes could literally save your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:15:57-07:00","id":1408287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408278#post1408278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even artifacts can <i>potentially</i> benefit - if you've banked enough craft xp, there's no <i>technical</i> reason you can't just roll every single crafting roll one after the other, virtually instantaneously. If you're trying to finish the daiklave made from the bone of his corpse that you've just found in his tomb, while actually <i>fighting</i> the First and Forsaken Lion, saving those motes could literally save your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a minimum duration between rolls. Even Solar charms only push it down to weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:44:28-07:00","id":1408293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408287#post1408287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a minimum duration between rolls. Even Solar charms only push it down to weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, this is not the case! It's definitely unusual compared to most extended rolls, but the craft rules are actually pretty clear - &quot;artifacts require a minimum time spent laboring over their construction before a character can attempt to finish them&quot;, but as a one-time thing only. &quot;The roll has <i>no set interval</i>; each time the character pays 10 gold points to attempt to complete the project, she can roll once, and may attempt her next roll once she can pay another 10 gold points to try again.&quot; (emphasis mine, all from &quot;Finishing a superior project&quot;, Exalted p. 241).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T19:32:52-07:00","id":1408304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408275#post1408275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is mote saving for rolls really worth it for craft ? I can't remember any time it was useful to track motes for crafting rolls</div> </div> </div> </div>I play a Craft Supernal Twilight and I've literally never needed to craft mid combat, and i only track motes spent on Craft in case I get ambushed midway through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T22:39:46-07:00","id":1408314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408304#post1408304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I play a Craft Supernal Twilight and I've literally never needed to craft mid combat, and i only track motes spent on Craft in case I get ambushed midway through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever had to craft and then less than four hours later gotten into some other manner of trouble?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T00:08:41-07:00","id":1408319,"title":"","content":"Pretty comprehensive answers all round.<br /> <br /> Anyone crafted any artifacts in play as a Deeb?<br /> <br /> (I've done a superior mundane crafting project. But with no Terminus, that's considerably easier.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T01:49:28-07:00","id":1408323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408314#post1408314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever had to craft and then less than four hours later gotten into some other manner of trouble?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? No. Despite how silly that sounds, when we sit around the table there's clearly marked down time, and that's when I go ham on the artifacts. CNNT lets you bust out anything simple instantly and there's nothing there that needs an Excellency. Vice Miracle Technique and Ever Ready Innovation cover your &quot;oh shit&quot; combat crafts. There's enough to keep me busy on downtime, but not so much that its ever been a problem. <br /> <br /> I mean, eventually I'll get jumped by the Wyld Hunt while crafting, but the mandatory timelimit on Artifacts is 6-Ess weeks for Artifacts under 4 dots, and that many -months- for A5 and N/A. Just the power tree is enough to do that in less than 5 roles, and its so spread out that it will only matter if my ST is planning on attacking me specifically after a big excellency. <br /> <br /> Even then, I'm E3 with no attuned artifacts (cobbler's children!), 10 motes isn't gonna swing a battle. Not to mention that personally I have enough blood apes to make a size 1 battlegroup. <br /> <br /> I'm sure it can come up, but if a Ninja Dynast is gonna assassinate me the best time is when I'm blowing of steam in a bathhouse doing drugs and eating peeled grapes from the soft hands of concubines, not in my room surrounded by demons and other dangerous anathema. <br /> <br /> YMMV though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T03:47:03-07:00","id":1408329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408323#post1408323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when we sit around the table there's clearly marked down time</div> </div> </div> </div>This is typical for most games.<br /> <br /> But, if you think about it, it probably shouldn't be typical for Exalted.<br /> <br /> It's not like the world is a peaceful, civilised place but once a year adventures dive into dungeons to fight dragons.<br /> <br /> &quot;Downtime&quot; is a pure game conceit in Exalted. There is no &quot;downtime&quot;: the Deathlords don't say &quot;well chaps, it's off season now. Hit the showers, train up, college world domination starts in June, and we'll be back in the fall&quot;. The Wyld Hunt doesn't close for summer.<br /> <br /> Every game I've run has had downtime. That superior project my Deeb completed was during downtime.<br /> <br /> But downtime is still a really weird idea for Exalted, if you stop and think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T04:42:26-07:00","id":1408332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408319#post1408319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone crafted any artifacts in play as a Deeb?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm currently working on an artifact and a complete repair under my belt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T05:58:59-07:00","id":1408340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408329#post1408329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is typical for most games.<br /> <br /> But, if you think about it, it probably shouldn't be typical for Exalted.<br /> <br /> It's not like the world is a peaceful, civilised place but once a year adventures dive into dungeons to fight dragons.<br /> <br /> &quot;Downtime&quot; is a pure game conceit in Exalted. There is no &quot;downtime&quot;: the Deathlords don't say &quot;well chaps, it's off season now. Hit the showers, train up, college world domination starts in June, and we'll be back in the fall&quot;. The Wyld Hunt doesn't close for summer.<br /> <br /> Every game I've run has had downtime. That superior project my Deeb completed was during downtime.<br /> <br /> But downtime is still a really weird idea for Exalted, if you stop and think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not limited to Craft. The rules dictate how long training new skills/attributes/charms/etc take because there's that idea that you should be off &quot;training in the mountains&quot; and doing the waterfall meditation thing between adventures, and why its supposed to take decades to reach E4 and at minimum a century to get E5 for prodigies. Thats why artifacts have this mandatory multi-month requirement thats based on Story-time and not Game-time. <br /> <br /> I don't play with that kind of &quot;its been 7 months since the adventure of Dragon's Palace, what have you been doing?&quot; style, but the book expects you too.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I agree. Exalted is a lot like a tv show with several days of action and months of inconsequential time between seasons. I guesss the world ending horrors taking queuing very seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 08-15-2020, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T07:14:09-07:00","id":1408349,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re both looking at it backwards. Of course nothing ever interrupts your downtime because \u201cdowntime\u201d by definition is the period between important things happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T07:29:18-07:00","id":1408352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408349#post1408349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You\u2019re both looking at it backwards. Of course nothing ever interrupts your downtime because \u201cdowntime\u201d by definition is the period between important things happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But how come you ONLY craft things when nothing interrupts you?<br /> <br /> Your character doesn't know that nothing is going to happen when they start crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T08:13:00-07:00","id":1408359,"title":"","content":"To be fair even with downtime a Storyteller is well within their rights to draw it to a close with something like &quot;as you quench your new daiklave, you see smoke on the horizon&quot;. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T08:21:33-07:00","id":1408360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408352#post1408352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. But how come you ONLY craft things when nothing interrupts you?<br /> <br /> Your character doesn't know that nothing is going to happen when they start crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably, your character does not start craft projects in the midst of other time-critical activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T08:32:54-07:00","id":1408362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408275#post1408275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is mote saving for rolls really worth it for craft ? I can't remember any time it was useful to track motes for crafting rolls</div> </div> </div> </div>There's less interaction between downtime and those charms than you think.<br /> <br /> Most are either committed or spent during the roll. <br /> Committed motes are a minor consideration, although committing too much means the character is spending himself dry all the time. Outside of peaceful times and places this may be a problem.<br /> <br /> Motes spent during the roll are critical for that day or three. It's a window of a few days where you are, essentially, on Deadline Mode. Burning yourself out to get the last touches done, concerned it may break apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> Either way both bring considerations that are relevant on camera, and bring considerations that are perennial in character. Most artisans will not start big demanding jobs if they can't have the peace of mind that they will be able to work mostly uninterruptedly. And interruptions may not be critical, but will there will be a sensible limitation anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T09:17:57-07:00","id":1408366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408360#post1408360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably, your character does not start craft projects in the midst of other time-critical activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>With charms like Craftsman Needs No Tools, and the general way the craft system works to incentivize crafting all the time, you're actually quite likely to be starting craft projects during time-critical activities. I already gave an example, upthread, of doing a major project to reinforce the gate of a besieged city just before the besiegers start battering at it, but I can think of many, many more examples. If the Circle is going to a fancy party in an hour but has nothing to wear, the Craft (Tailoring) specialist whips them all up some fancy formal wear. In a village under threat from floods, the Craft (Masonry) character builds a wall to divert the floodwaters at lightning speed. The Circle is ambushed in a teahouse by the Wyld Hunt, and their weapons are all somewhere else. The Craft (Weaponsmithing) person proceeds to cobble together tablelegs, sharp shards of pottery, and tablecloths as handle wrapping, and rapidly creates swords for everyone, so nobody has to deal with the improvised weapon penalty. And so on. <br /> <br /> And the Dragon-Blooded get craft speed enhancing charms too (Stone-Carving Fingers, for example), even if they're not as versatile or <i>quite</i> as fast as the Solar ones, so they can do similar sorts of craft tricks, and want to save motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:20:37-07:00","id":1408373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408360#post1408360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably, your character does not start craft projects in the midst of other time-critical activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last week two of our PCs had a lumberjack contest in <i>the same day</i> another PC was targeted by the Wyld Hunt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:23:26-07:00","id":1408374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408360#post1408360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably, your character does not start craft projects in the midst of other time-critical activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But that's exactly my point! Exactly my point&quot; ~ Mouse<br /> <br /> Your character's knowledge of when they are in the midsts of a time-critical activity isn't perfect.<br /> <br /> You don't know if the Wyld Hunt has found you, or the Mask of Winters's deathknights are three days away, or if Raksi is about to unleash her latest horror on the world, or whatever you are using as plot. You know (maybe) that nothing is happening <i>right now</i>, but not that your schedule is free for the next two months.<br /> <br /> Obviously if the Wyld Hunt sets fire to your workshop, you know now <i>isn't</i> a great time. But how do you infallibly know when <i>is</i> a good time?<br /> <br /> The Empress is missing, the Deathlords walk Creation, the Solars have returned... if the ST asks &quot;how do you spend the next six weeks&quot;, the characters have no way of knowing that they've got six hassle free weeks ahead.<br /> <br /> (I think the best way of doing it is probably for the ST to decide in secret how much downtime there's going to be, and have the PCs declare what they're doing on a week by week basis. But this almost deserves its own thread at this point.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-15-2020, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T11:06:09-07:00","id":1408384,"title":"","content":"The real mote management problem for DB crafters is the Charms with a duration of \u201cOne project.\u201d Plot happening between artifact rolls while you have 15m committed to Eternal Omphalos or Dragon-Smith sounds like a bad time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T18:53:08-07:00","id":1408439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408384#post1408384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real mote management problem for DB crafters is the Charms with a duration of \u201cOne project.\u201d Plot happening between artifact rolls while you have 15m committed to Eternal Omphalos or Dragon-Smith sounds like a bad time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the real issue here- committing motes to months long charms is going to leave you disadvantaged, especially for a DeeB. Blowing a full excellency and using a few charms for a craft roll isn't really a big deal. <br /> <br /> A Crafter getting jumped mid craft is comparable to a Face getting jumped after a big social scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T21:11:02-07:00","id":1408455,"title":"","content":"Though now that I think about it you can pretty much just pretend that Blazing Dragon-Smith Arete is instant duration since it doesn\u2019t cost any craft points or have a cooldown, so it\u2019s really just an Eternal Omphalos Forge problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 08-16-2020, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T23:11:30-07:00","id":1408462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408329#post1408329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathlords don't say &quot;well chaps, it's off season now. Hit the showers, train up, college world domination starts in June, and we'll be back in the fall&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Picturing this made me laugh out lout for real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408439#post1408439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Crafter getting jumped mid craft is comparable to a Face getting jumped after a big social scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this not happen to people? It happens to me all the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think my perspective may be a bit skewed though, as most of the craft rolls I've seen have been quick ones in response to current problems. Like one time in a game I had a bunch of Solar PCs come up to what they thought was an ancient temple, only to realize that millenia of time passing had buried it. Guess who didn't bring shovels? The Twilight had to CNNT up a bunch of them to let the group dig out the entrance. There's been a few times when somebody took a longass time to make some big project, but more often than not it's been somebody pounding out a basic or major project to fix a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T01:39:23-07:00","id":1408465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408462#post1408462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Picturing this made me laugh out lout for real.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does this not happen to people? It happens to me all the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think my perspective may be a bit skewed though, as most of the craft rolls I've seen have been quick ones in response to current problems. Like one time in a game I had a bunch of Solar PCs come up to what they thought was an ancient temple, only to realize that millenia of time passing had buried it. Guess who didn't bring shovels? The Twilight had to CNNT up a bunch of them to let the group dig out the entrance. There's been a few times when somebody took a longass time to make some big project, but more often than not it's been somebody pounding out a basic or major project to fix a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In case of mundane craft it has happened, but in case of real Crafting projects I've never had this situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:06:56-07:00","id":1408591,"title":"","content":"Downtime is just time that no crisis (that can't be dealt with a simplified roll) happens. In my case, downtime is an accorded time that happens whenever the players complain loudly that they need more time to spend their exp and buy charms and skills.<br /> <br /> They usually do split their every day's time to do stuff, though. So, if they are crafting something, they spend eight hours every day on it (even adventure time), unless circumstances impede this. This applies to time spent training as well. The players have google sheets for every day, it's very organized. Some of them have invested heavily in the meditation charms to squeeze more time to build and grow (months sleeping only 5 minutes a day). They are the workaholic exalted. Fortunately, they have a handy lunar seneschal to offload the administration tasks, or else the kingdom would suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T15:45:41-07:00","id":1408603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408462#post1408462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picturing this made me laugh out lout for real.</div> </div> </div> </div>*designs a deathlord that acts like that*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T17:07:44-07:00","id":1408616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408603#post1408603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *designs a deathlord that acts like that*</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think fair number might do something like that. Probably more formal language, but the idea is sound. If you're in the South, you don't want to march an army during Summer. The same for the North and the Winter. Similar for marching during rainy seasons when roads are mud, or sailing through a monsoon. Underworld-travel, undead armies and Exalted can minimize this, but you have a significant number of mortal soldiers (or sorcerers, necromancers, generals, occultist, camp followers, etc), or abyssal without resistance charms there are times of year you can't do military operations. Why not tell your minions when the mission starts, and to find something to do until then.<br /> Also, making zombie armies probably takes time. If your current army gets destroyed, everyone who doesn't know how to make zombies gets some time where they can't do anything zombie-army-related","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T17:39:02-07:00","id":1408620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408352#post1408352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how come you ONLY craft things when nothing interrupts you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do it when you're in a friendly country that has borders lying a few weeks away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character doesn't know that nothing is going to happen when they start crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically, something that does happen is going to take a while to come to one's attention in many cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408340#post1408340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I agree. Exalted is a lot like a tv show with several days of action and months of inconsequential time between seasons. I guesss the world ending horrors taking queuing very seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>The world is big and the horrors are small. You dealt with your horror this season; the Mask of Winters is the problem of the Exalted and other powers living in the Scavenger Lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T00:27:24-07:00","id":1408660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408620#post1408620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could do it when you're in a friendly country that has borders lying a few weeks away.</div> </div> </div> </div>And during that time, you start your craft project knowing for a fact that their won't be a drought, or an assassination, or that burglars won't try and rob you, or that none of the gods of the kingdom's mortal lovers will die, or the volcano won't erupt?<br /> <br /> But all of these things and more will happen just as soon as you spend those last 10WhP?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Logically, something that does happen is going to take a while to come to one's attention in many cases. </div> </div> </div>Right. The Wyld Hunt has been tracking you for three months, but you don't find out until three days after you defeat the Mask of Winters.<br /> <br /> The things that &quot;take a while to come to your attention&quot; are exactly the things that could disrupt your crafting projects.<br /> <br /> It's not unrealistic to have two months where nothing noteworthy happens. But I maintain that it is unrealistic to flawlessly predict when these downtime periods are going to be, and to ONLY start Craft projects when you KNOW you won't be interrupted.<br /> <br /> Contrast with the Projects system, which all but guarentees that SOMETHING will go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-17-2020, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T00:46:33-07:00","id":1408663,"title":"","content":"Even taking all that to heart, there are only about 5 rolls to make an artifact spread out over a period of Weeks or Months. So if you just happen to get jumped in the extremely narrow timeframe of &quot;a few hours after a big Craft excellency&quot; its probably ST fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T01:00:26-07:00","id":1408664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408663#post1408663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even taking all that to heart, there are only about 5 rolls to make an artifact spread out over a period of Weeks or Months. So if you just happen to get jumped in the extremely narrow timeframe of &quot;a few hours after a big Craft excellency&quot; its probably ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the thing disrupting your plans isn't something directly antagonistic towards you. Which can happen, Tsutomu Yamaguchi was in Hiroshima on August 6th 1945, he survived the bomb and decided to go home. To Nagaski. On August 9th 1945.<br /> <br /> If the thing disrupting your plans is intelligently antagonistic towards you, then waiting until you're exhausted after a long day of smithing is a pretty likely moment to strike. I certainly wouldn't call BS on my players for doing that to an antagonist that they knew was crafting something big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T01:29:32-07:00","id":1408669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408663#post1408663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even taking all that to heart, there are only about 5 rolls to make an artifact spread out over a period of Weeks or Months. So if you just happen to get jumped in the extremely narrow timeframe of &amp;quot;a few hours after a big Craft excellency&amp;quot; its probably ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you're spending Willpower, that certainly can leave you down.<br /> <br /> (But I'm actually happy with the ST fiat thing. I realise I've posted a lot on this, but I don't feel strongly about it -- as I said, my only 3E superior project happened in downtime.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T01:49:33-07:00","id":1408672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408660#post1408660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And during that time, you start your craft project knowing for a fact that their won't be a drought, or an assassination, or that burglars won't try and rob you, or that none of the gods of the kingdom's mortal lovers will die, or the volcano won't erupt?<br /> <br /> But all of these things and more will happen just as soon as you spend those last 10WhP?<br /> <br /> <br /> Right. The Wyld Hunt has been tracking you for three months, but you don't find out until three days after you defeat the Mask of Winters.<br /> <br /> The things that &quot;take a while to come to your attention&quot; are exactly the things that could disrupt your crafting projects.<br /> <br /> It's not unrealistic to have two months where nothing noteworthy happens. But I maintain that it is unrealistic to flawlessly predict when these downtime periods are going to be, and to ONLY start Craft projects when you KNOW you won't be interrupted.<br /> <br /> Contrast with the Projects system, which all but guarentees that SOMETHING will go wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to remember that for a lot of people, downtimes are an agreement between the ST and players to let them do &quot;the things that take time&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T02:03:31-07:00","id":1408676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408672#post1408672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's important to remember that for a lot of people, downtimes are an agreement between the ST and players to let them do &quot;the things that take time&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>But THAT is the point.<br /> <br /> These things take time, and cost motes and willpower, for a reason.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;The time this takes doesn't matter, go nuts&quot; each and every time, IMHO, is missing the point. Unless there's some kind of trade off (like taking a month off to build a Daiklave means Mnemon gets a month off the countdown to doom whereby she unlocks the Imperial Manse), why have downtime at all? Why not just give the PCs what they want for free?<br /> <br /> If all Crafting is always free and never interrupted, then why put costs on Craft Charms?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not against crafting during downtime. So long as you're also crafting during play <i>with a meaningful chance of getting interrupted</i> (spending 10 seconds to CNNT something without so much as spending 1m on an Excellency doesn't count).<br /> <br /> Otherwise downtime becomes a cudgel to bludgeon your players with. &quot;Can we have some downtime to-&quot; &quot;NO!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm okay with an ST saying &quot;What do you want to do? Build a Daiklave? Okay, that's fine -- I don't want to play that out so let's take some downtime.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I don't want to be in a position as ST where I can't put some downtime in my stories without the PCs popping out five new artifacts now they know they can do it in perfect safety. And as a player, I don't want to only be able Craft things between stories when the ST says so.<br /> <br /> If you're blowing all your motes on something (combat, crafting, a social scene) then that leaves you vulnerable and limited. For me, that's an important part of the Exalted experience -- your power is not unlimited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-17-2020, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T02:37:16-07:00","id":1408681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408676#post1408676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But THAT is the point.<br /> <br /> These things take time, and cost motes and willpower, for a reason.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;The time this takes doesn't matter, go nuts&quot; each and every time, IMHO, is missing the point. Unless there's some kind of trade off (like taking a month off to build a Daiklave means Mnemon gets a month off the countdown to doom whereby she unlocks the Imperial Manse), why have downtime at all? Why not just give the PCs what they want for free?<br /> <br /> If all Crafting is always free and never interrupted, then why put costs on Craft Charms?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not against crafting during downtime. So long as you're also crafting during play <i>with a meaningful chance of getting interrupted</i> (spending 10 seconds to CNNT something without so much as spending 1m on an Excellency doesn't count).<br /> <br /> Otherwise downtime becomes a cudgel to bludgeon your players with. &quot;Can we have some downtime to-&quot; &quot;NO!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm okay with an ST saying &quot;What do you want to do? Build a Daiklave? Okay, that's fine -- I don't want to play that out so let's take some downtime.&quot;<br /> <br /> But I don't want to be in a position as ST where I can't put some downtime in my stories without the PCs popping out five new artifacts now they know they can do it in perfect safety. And as a player, I don't want to only be able Craft things between stories when the ST says so.<br /> <br /> If you're blowing all your motes on something (combat, crafting, a social scene) then that leaves you vulnerable and limited. For me, that's an important part of the Exalted experience -- your power is not unlimited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally I'd agree with you but the time frames of many groups may vary easily. If my players and I didn't agree on downtime during my first campaign the crafter might never had the opportunity to craft anything since we did all Essence 1-2 into the timespan of 1 months. Since players got so many ways to go fast and furious, they might decide it's not worth to take the time for something because they have the abilities to be always on the move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T03:35:25-07:00","id":1408684,"title":"","content":"This discussion seems to be getting away from the original question and into territory of GM adjudication of downtime.<br /> <br /> As far as the original question: Dragonblooded are mechanically capable of Crafting, but I think the fact that, for the most part, they've got to actually go and use all of those Intervals and care about Terminus. This can be intimidating, because most players who aren't coming into Dragonblooded blind are familiar at least passingly with Solars casually snapping the craft system over their golden knees. (as an aside, the craft supernal in the game i'm running is up to 165 Artifacts crafted). Seeing the lower numbers and less impressive dice tricks can be discouraging, but fret not! Dragonblooded are totally capable of Crafting even 5 dot artifacts, once their Essence is high enough.<br /> <br /> Just don't try for First Age Artifice. Seriously. You're never going to get enough white xp. It's not gonna happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T03:48:36-07:00","id":1408685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408660#post1408660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And during that time, you start your craft project knowing for a fact that their won't be a drought, or an assassination, or that burglars won't try and rob you, or that none of the gods of the kingdom's mortal lovers will die, or the volcano won't erupt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jeez, how do your Exalted ever feel comfortable enough to sleep at night?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But all of these things and more will happen just as soon as you spend those last 10WhP?</div> </div> </div> </div>That they will happen when somewhat convenient is the benefit of being a dramatically inclined game rather than some kind of simulation.<br /> <br /> That characters ever feel comfortable enough to do things other than feel constantly on the edge of disaster is presumably because they're... normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I maintain that it is unrealistic to flawlessly predict when these downtime periods are going to be, and to ONLY start Craft projects when you KNOW you won't be interrupted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a flawless prediction. It's a reasonably informed prediction that is validated by the omnipotence of the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> I'm saying this as somebody who actually would feel that significant craft projects would be well suited to coincide with the active scenes in some manner. I just think your refutations are taking things to a bit absurd extremes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T04:23:45-07:00","id":1408688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408685#post1408685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jeez, how do your Exalted ever feel comfortable enough to sleep at night?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That they will happen when somewhat convenient is the benefit of being a dramatically inclined game rather than some kind of simulation.<br /> <br /> That characters ever feel comfortable enough to do things other than feel constantly on the edge of disaster is presumably because they're... normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not a flawless prediction. It's a reasonably informed prediction that is validated by the omnipotence of the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> I'm saying this as somebody who actually would feel that significant craft projects would be well suited to coincide with the active scenes in some manner. I just think your refutations are taking things to a bit absurd extremes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're talking past each other.<br /> <br /> Of course the characters feel safe. But there's a big dramatic difference between feeling safe and being totally invulnerable to harm.<br /> <br /> There's downtime between A New Hope and Empire Strikes Back. The rebels set up a new base, Han settles in. But it's not the case that everything goes perfectly and the plot only starts up again once all loose ends have been resolved.<br /> <br /> Of course your PCs should feel safe enough to start a project between pressing adventures. My contention is simply that they shouldn't know perfectly how long they will be safe for in order to maximise concequence-free artifact construction.<br /> <br /> Extending that line of thinking to say my characters should dread going to sleep at night is &quot;taking things to absurd extremes&quot;.<br /> <br /> The sum total of my argument is that I don't think that <i>infallibly</i> the world comes to a screeching halt every time you sit down in your workshop. If you take umbridge with that, then such is your right. But I expect we've been bull's rushed into semantics at this point.<br /> <br /> I think Lioness said it best. All I'm advocating is that <i>occassionally</i> things like this happen:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408359#post1408359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair even with downtime a Storyteller is well within their rights to draw it to a close with something like &amp;quot;as you quench your new daiklave, you see smoke on the horizon&amp;quot;. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-17-2020, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T05:32:43-07:00","id":1408694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408684#post1408684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion seems to be getting away from the original question and into territory of GM adjudication of downtime.<br /> <br /> As far as the original question: Dragonblooded are mechanically capable of Crafting, but I think the fact that, for the most part, they've got to actually go and use all of those Intervals and care about Terminus. This can be intimidating, because most players who aren't coming into Dragonblooded blind are familiar at least passingly with Solars casually snapping the craft system over their golden knees. (as an aside, the craft supernal in the game i'm running is up to 165 Artifacts crafted). Seeing the lower numbers and less impressive dice tricks can be discouraging, but fret not! Dragonblooded are totally capable of Crafting even 5 dot artifacts, once their Essence is high enough.<br /> <br /> Just don't try for First Age Artifice. Seriously. You're never going to get enough white xp. It's not gonna happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an aside : is this why the Empress accumulates so much Jade ? To help maintain artifacts for the Dragon-Blooded Dynasty ? Or is this just for money ? I never understood why there is so much focus on Jade from The Realm in the core books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T06:28:08-07:00","id":1408701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408694#post1408694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an aside : is this why the Empress accumulates so much Jade ? To help maintain artifacts for the Dragon-Blooded Dynasty ? Or is this just for money ? I never understood why there is so much focus on Jade from The Realm in the core books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jade is valuable because it's magical and rare.<br /> <br /> Controlling the supply of jade means controlling artifacts (which is as much about restricting supply to your enemies as it is creating supply for your allies) and it gives you an inherently stable currency.<br /> <br /> Historically, RL kingdoms would accumulate gold. Jade has all the advantages that gold had in real life... and can also be used to do magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T06:37:12-07:00","id":1408702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408701#post1408701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jade is valuable because it's magical and rare.<br /> <br /> Controlling the supply of jade means controlling artifacts (which is as much about restricting supply to your enemies as it is creating supply for your allies) and it gives you an inherently stable currency.<br /> <br /> Historically, RL kingdoms would accumulate gold. Jade has all the advantages that gold had in real life... and can also be used to do magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but do we agree the only magic you can come up with Jade is Artifacts ? I'm not saying it's a bad thing, I just had the feeling The Realm had so much artifacts already, and you need to be an Exalted to manipulate one, that they couldn't do much with more Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:08:42-07:00","id":1408707,"title":"","content":"You can always use more artifacts.<br /> <br /> Artifacts aren't just fancy swords. They can change the weather, transport goods, harvest crops, heal the sick, feed the hungry.<br /> <br /> And, in 3E, artifacts are a lot rarer than in 2E. Not every Dynast has a magic sword.<br /> <br /> And it's very useful to make sure the Threshold kingdoms DON'T have jade to make artifacts, because they've had to pay it all to the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:31:37-07:00","id":1408709,"title":"","content":"They definitely benefit from hoarding jade as far as stifling opposition goes, that's for sure. I bet there's lots of spywork for and against them in the form of stealing jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:43:07-07:00","id":1408713,"title":"","content":"I also advocate for things to happen mid-project simply because it gives the sense of the passage of time better. It\u2019s why I like to have a little backup book of sea adventures handy. Any time the players take a 4 month sea voyage it often ends up taking an actual session or two because of stuff along the way.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re building a massive blue water ship, you can expect that at some point your supply of lumber will come under attack by rogue gods or thieves or something. That way two actual weeks have passed in real life since you started building the ship, and also it builds in a nice little bit of story for the obstacles you overcame to construct it.<br /> <br /> Maybe not every single time, but pretty much for any long project. Short projects usually end up being done mid-action anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:52:57-07:00","id":1408716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408707#post1408707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can always use more artifacts.<br /> <br /> Artifacts aren't just fancy swords. They can change the weather, transport goods, harvest crops, heal the sick, feed the hungry.<br /> <br /> And, in 3E, artifacts are a lot rarer than in 2E. Not every Dynast has a magic sword.<br /> <br /> And it's very useful to make sure the Threshold kingdoms DON'T have jade to make artifacts, because they've had to pay it all to the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think I just haven't seen a lot of content describing the importance of controlling the Artifact economy, but I haven't finished reading The Realm yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T07:54:14-07:00","id":1408718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408439#post1408439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Crafter getting jumped mid craft is comparable to a Face getting jumped after a big social scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is sometimes appropriate. Especially when the attacker is weaker than the player character and there's an internal reasoning to why they'd wait for a moment like this in order to strike rather than the optimised Day Caste assassin appearing at the worst possible time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T09:17:19-07:00","id":1408731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408702#post1408702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but do we agree the only magic you can come up with Jade is Artifacts ? I'm not saying it's a bad thing, I just had the feeling The Realm had so much artifacts already, and you need to be an Exalted to manipulate one, that they couldn't do much with more Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to wanting more artifacts (to replace lost artifacts, deal with population growth, get a personalized artifact instead of one made for someone else), Manses require jade - given the description of jade currency, they need multiple talents weighing 68lb a piece.<br /> <br /> It's also possible there are lesser magical objects that are made from jade - talismans and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T10:36:33-07:00","id":1408742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408716#post1408716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I think I just haven't seen a lot of content describing the importance of controlling the Artifact economy, but I haven't finished reading The Realm yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the regular economy. Jade is expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T11:19:54-07:00","id":1408751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408742#post1408742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the regular economy. Jade is expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah but I fail to see how it is expensive if it's not very useful. But I just suck at economy, I don't get why gold was so valuable in western history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T12:41:30-07:00","id":1408768,"title":"","content":"The very broad over generalization?<br /> <br /> Stability, on a few levels.<br /> <br /> Materials that are physically stable for extremely long periods of time can be locked up in vaults without much worry. If you can level a slab of [stuff] in an vault for 200 years and not have any noticeable physical decay, that's a very useful trait for items meant to signify wealth. Gold doesn't react much, so it can sit there for ages and still be the same amount of gold. Leaving a bunch of iron bars in the same circumstances could mean having a room full of rust.<br /> <br /> Materials that have low amounts of practical applications mean that hording them to measure wealth is less is less disruptive to actual work. Gold sitting around in a vault isn't making it harder for your farmers to farm. Iron sitting around in a vault isn't being turned into tools for farmers to use to grow more crops.<br /> <br /> How useful low utility materials are is generally stable. Gold rarely changes in how useful it is (because it generally isn't), and thus its value is stable. How useful iron is can change radically based on circumstance. During peace, iron might be cheap because you're just making/replacing tools, but if a war breaks out and you need to start making steel weapons, iron becomes very expensive.<br /> <br /> Humans are incredibly irrational (not a bad thing, but a lot of economic theories tend to assume the opposite) when it comes to assessing the value of wealth. We put value on things that have nothing to do with any sort of practical application. Shiny pretty baubles are more desirable so we'll value them more even though they add nothing to practical value. Slap a celebrity's name on something and people will attach greater value to it. Etc. This is, ultimately, predictable and thus another form of stability. How much we like sparkly rocks tends to persist easily with some simple cultural normalization; far more so than many other sources of emotional value. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T13:21:58-07:00","id":1408780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408751#post1408751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but I fail to see how it is expensive if it's not very useful. But I just suck at economy, I don't get why gold was so valuable in western history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, all of this is just from a layman's perspective - I do not have a degree in economics or anything! So, usual disclaimer about taking the word of a stranger on the Internet. :-)<br /> <br /> That said, here's an attempt to explain. Money is generally held to have three major functions, which a currency needs at <i>least</i> one of, and ideally more than that, and the better it is at one or more of these functions, the better it is as money. These functions are a <i>medium of exchange</i>, a <i>measure of value</i>, and a <i>store of value</i>.<br /> <br /> A medium of exchange means that the item can be practically exchanged for other things. If you can say &quot;I will give you this thing, in exchange for that other thing you have that I want&quot;, then the thing fulfills this function. This doesn't have to mean something physically changes hands, note! There's a somewhat famous example, the island of Yap in the Pacific Ocean, where wealth was traditionally measured by ownership of huge stone wheels. These couldn't be physically moved without great effort, but <i>ownership</i> of them could be transferred, with one person saying &quot;I will give you ownership of my giant stone wheel in exchange for your daughter's hand in marriage&quot;, for example. The wheel wasn't moved, but ownership was publicly transferred, and thus wealth was as well. One quality that makes something good for this function is how divisible it is - can you divide it into smaller portions in order to pay for smaller things, and still have those smaller portions recognized as valuable? Precious materials tend to be good for this, particularly if you can also recombine them - one tenth of an ounce of gold is generally regarded as one tenth the value of an ounce of gold, and ten one-tenth ounces can easily be recombined into an ounce.<br /> <br /> Something serves as a measure of value if it's something that is generally recognized as valuable, something that many people will want, at least at <i>some</i> point, and have to expend effort to get. This tends to rule out substances or services that are extremely freely available. In most places on Earth or Creation, water wouldn't serve as a good measure of value, because its too easy to just walk out and grab it where it's freely available. Stuff that's rare or takes a fair bit of effort to obtain, on the other hand, makes a better measure of value. On Earth, precious metals met this criteria, because people tended to value them for their beauty, and because they were relatively rare and took a fair bit of work to find and obtain.<br /> <br /> The function of being a <i>store</i> of value means that you can obtain the thing, and keep it until you need it, without it losing too much of its value. That way, instead of exchanging it for whatever else you need immediately, you can keep it somewhere, and use it when you really need it. This function is one reason that food items, despite generally meeting the other two categories, are more rare as money - food tends to degrade over time, even when carefully stored. If your economy is all based on apples, you risk losing your stored wealth when worms get into your apple barrels. This isn't universal, note: there are definitely examples of food being used as the basis for money. But they tend to be food that is easier to store long-term, and often diverge from being <i>strictly</i> food-based in any case. Precious metals like gold, of course, meet this criteria quite well, since they tend to be resistant to damage and erosion. Gold is particularly good for it, because gold doesn't even tarnish the way silver does, meaning gold will always be shiny and beautiful, not even requiring effort to keep it polished. Another thing that makes things better for this function is that if they're not subject to large swings in production - if your currency is based on something that you don't know how much of will be available at any given time, that makes things more uncertain. That's another reason non-perishable stuff like precious metals tends to be a better choice than food - food's a lot more inherently variable in how much will be available at any given time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Note that these functions, <i>particularly</i> the &quot;measure of value&quot; one, can actually become rather self-fulfilling. If something is chosen as a medium of exchange, people are likely to find ways of preserving it more effectively, and it <i>definitely</i> tends to accrue value, even if it wasn't perceived as valuable before. There's theories that gold and other precious metals weren't nearly as valuable before various states started using them as mediums of exchange - essentially, it's not that gold is used as money because it's valuable, it's that gold is valuable <i>because</i> it's used as money.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, jade fulfills all three functions above reasonably well, hence why it makes sense as a currency. It's transferable, both on paper and physically, and it can be reasonably easily subdivided and recombined without losing significant value, making it a good medium of exchange. It's a decent measure of value, because it's rare enough and requires enough work to find, but not <i>so</i> rare as to be difficult to get enough to use, and it has inherent utility, being useful for being made into artifacts. And it's an <i>extremely</i> good <i>store</i> of value, being inherently hard to damage and resistant to corrosion and such, and with the supply being relatively constant. So, all told, basing an economy on jade is not a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T15:57:58-07:00","id":1408800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1408186-can-dragon-blooded-craft-artifacts?p=1408751#post1408751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but I fail to see how it is expensive if it's not very useful. But I just suck at economy, I don't get why gold was so valuable in western history.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to the above notes, gold fulfills a few useful simultaneous categories: it's rare enough that it's in limited supply, common enough that it's practical for use in the quantities that being used as currency requires, and has a melting point that can be reached with nothing but an open flame, meaning it can easily be shaped into coins or ingots of consistent size even with very little technology and without losing much if any gold in the process. Coins made out of stone or wood would require substantially more effort to manufacture to a consistent standard.<br /> <br /> Jade is actually not analagous to gold in this regard, since it has to be cut rather than melted and this is explicitly a lossy process, but in jade's case this is made up for by the ability to alloy jade dust with metals for creating artifacts, so the solid jade lost in the process of converting between currency formats still has value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T20:33:57-07:00","id":1408840,"title":"","content":"Though the one form of specie currency used for the longest time and over the greatest area and by the largest total population is not any precious metal, but the cowrie shell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T21:26:01-07:00","id":1408851,"title":"","content":"The problem with &quot;practically useful&quot; things is that the demand for &quot;practically useful&quot; things is subject to satisfaction. On the other hand, the demand for a status symbol is effectively infinite under normal circumstances, because human psychology is such that (almost) everyone (almost) always wants more status. That gold and cowrie shells have no use except showing off how high-status a human you are made them good candidates for money. Jade not being all that useful (but, insofar as it is, useful for something that's a status marker in the part of Realm society that has the most time and resources for playing status games) is consistent with this.<br /> <br /> And while this is surface-irrational, it still comes from a logical place. Both survival and reproductive success for most people in most of human history have been <i>hugely</i> dependent on social status; peer pressure works because being shunned was historically a very good way to not have descendants. Even in societies with marked, generationally-persistent castes, your status in the internal society of your caste was vitally important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T00:59:24-07:00","id":1408872,"title":"","content":"Well thanks for your answers I think I have a better understanding of the subject now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}